<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southern Transitional Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2017–</span> · Also known as STC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Southern Transitional Council is a southern Yemeni separatist organisation formed in May 2017 under Aidarus al-Zoubaidi, the dismissed governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, and backed by the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>. It seeks an independent southern state. Its forces seized Aden from the recognised government in 2019, and it joined the Presidential Leadership Council in 2022 while keeping its own armed forces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southern-transitional-council.jpg" alt="Southern Transitional Council" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Southern Transitional Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Yemen_(Non-standard_Variant).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
